Description: pvr: reuse control stream buffers
 Every control stream buffer of a command buffer is a separate 4 KiB buffer
 object: pvr_csb_buffer_extend() creates, CPU-maps and GPU-maps one with
 pvr_bo_alloc(), and pvr_csb_finish() and the free of a graphics sub command
 unmap and destroy it again. With render states cached, buffer objects are
 still created, mapped and destroyed for every submit under zink, each costing
 PVR_CREATE_BO, PVR_GET_BO_MMAP_OFFSET, mmap, PVR_VM_MAP and on release
 PVR_VM_UNMAP, munmap and GEM_CLOSE; every graphics and compute sub command
 allocates at least one control stream buffer.
 .
 Keep released control stream buffers in a per-device pool of up to 256
 buffers (1 MiB) and take from it in pvr_csb_buffer_extend() before
 allocating. pvr_csb_finish() and the release of the baked terminate and view
 index control streams return the buffers to the pool. A reused buffer is
 cleared, so it has the same contents as a new one. Buffers are released only
 when the command buffer is reset or freed, which requires that it is not
 pending, so a pooled buffer is not in use by the GPU. The pool is emptied in
 device destruction after the render state cache.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
